          "guid": "mt0u6st2zd6u29dt",
          "message": {
            "text": "This conversion restores Blink internal paint coordinates rather than fitting pixels. At Chromium 7d859f271c, ConvertBorderWidth and ConvertOutlineOffset store effective-zoomed integer lengths, while CSSValueFromComputedStyleInternal serializes through ZoomAdjustedPixelValue. Domotion combines those CSSOM strings with already-physical DOMRects, so multiplying once by the ancestor effective zoom is the missing inverse. The DSF 1/2 × zoom 0.8/1.25 phase matrix moved from 309 failures to 9 without changing an envelope; both DSF=2 rows became 128/128 and every HTML/SVG snap classification now agrees.",
            "markdown": "This conversion restores Blink internal paint coordinates rather than fitting pixels. At Chromium 7d859f271c, ConvertBorderWidth and ConvertOutlineOffset store effective-zoomed integer lengths, while CSSValueFromComputedStyleInternal serializes through ZoomAdjustedPixelValue. Domotion combines those CSSOM strings with already-physical DOMRects, so multiplying once by the ancestor effective zoom is the missing inverse. The DSF 1/2 × zoom 0.8/1.25 phase matrix moved from 309 failures to 9 without changing an envelope; both DSF=2 rows became 128/128 and every HTML/SVG snap classification now agrees."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/capture/script/walker/borders-backgrounds.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 51,
                  "endLine": 63,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "/** Computed border/outline lengths are serialized in pre-effective-zoom CSS\n * pixels, while captured DOMRects are already in painted coordinates. Blink's\n * paint code consumes the zoomed ComputedStyle value, so cross that boundary\n * exactly once during capture. Chromium 7d859f271c:\n * StyleBuilderConverter::{ConvertBorderWidth,ConvertOutlineOffset} stores\n * zoomed integer lengths; longhands_custom.cc serializes them through\n * ZoomAdjustedPixelValue before getComputedStyle exposes them. */\nexport const physicalComputedPaintLength = (value, effectiveZoom) => {\n  if (effectiveZoom === 1) return value;\n  const number = parseFloat(value);\n  if (!Number.isFinite(number)) return value;\n  return `${Math.round(number * effectiveZoom * 1e6) / 1e6}px`;\n};"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
